---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Quote from '../components/Quote.astro';
import { kindWords } from '../site';

const path = [
  {
    org: 'Ordergroove',
    when: '2026 to now',
    role: 'Principal Product Manager',
    note: 'Subscriptions and memberships for enterprise brands. I’m working on the future of payments in relationship commerce and where AI agents fit in.',
  },
  {
    org: 'Paramount Commerce',
    when: '2026',
    role: 'Staff Product Manager',
    note: 'Built a merchant hierarchy for a legacy payments platform. Not my favourite stretch.',
  },
  {
    org: 'Shopify',
    when: '2014 to 2025',
    role: '',
    note: 'Eleven years, from merchant support to product leadership.',
  },
  {
    org: '',
    when: '2024 to 2025',
    role: 'Product Lead, Shop and Shop Pay',
    note: 'Payments, identity, merchant APIs, and agentic commerce for tens of millions of buyers.',
  },
  {
    org: '',
    when: '2022 to 2024',
    role: 'Senior Product Manager, Shop Pay',
    note: 'Took Shop Pay to merchants off Shopify for the first time, launching with Everlane. Later moved to Shop Pay Installments and on-platform growth.',
  },
  {
    org: '',
    when: '2017 to 2022',
    role: 'Product Manager, Tax',
    note: 'Owned the tax platform (in-house calculation engine, reporting, Avalara partnership).',
  },
  {
    org: '',
    when: '2014 to 2017',
    role: 'Support, launch, and solutions engineering',
    note: 'Started as a support Guru, then onboarded and scoped Shopify Plus merchants. Top solutions engineer of 2016.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="About Brian Donohue: customer problems, teams, payments and tax, and what he does when he’s not working.">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      I like hard problems with a customer on the other end. I started my career answering support
      calls, and I still start every problem by asking who’s stuck and why.
    </p>

    <p>
      Most of those problems have been in commerce, so I know payments, wallets, and tax deeply.
      That helps. What I’m best at is the work around it: figuring out what customers need and
      getting engineering, design, data, and partners working on the same problem. Then I turn the
      mess into a simple system people can build on.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If I can’t explain who something helps and what it fixes for them, it isn’t ready to
        build.
      </li>
      <li>
        Most of my effort goes into getting people to agree on the problem. The solution usually
        moves faster after that.
      </li>
      <li>
        I build clear models of messy systems so teams can make a decision once and stop
        relitigating it every week.
      </li>
      <li>I’d rather say the awkward thing early than watch it come up in a retro.</li>
      <li>I joke around a fair bit, and I still do what I said I’d do.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <section class="path">
    <h2 class="label">Path</h2>
    <ol>
      {
        path.map((p) => (
          <li class={p.org ? 'org' : 'sub'}>
            <div class="head">
              <span class="role">
                {p.org && <strong>{p.org}</strong>}
                {p.org && p.role && <span class="sep"> · </span>}
                {p.role}
              </span>
              <span class="when">{p.when}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="note">{p.note}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
    <p class="more">
      I moved from support into product, and I’m always happy to talk with people trying to make
      that jump.
    </p>
    <p class="more">
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/brian-donohue-a61357114/">LinkedIn</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="kind">
    <h2 class="label">Kind words</h2>
    <div class="quotes">
      {kindWords.filter((k) => !k.featured).map((k) => <Quote {...k} small />)}
    </div>
    <p class="more">
      From <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/brian-donohue-a61357114/details/recommendations/"
        >recommendations on LinkedIn</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Off the clock</h2>
    <p>
      I race and maintain <a href="/projects/hardtack/">Hardtack</a>, a 1976 C&C 33. It’s a
      racer-cruiser, and about half of it is a repair list. I teach crew in more detail than they probably
      want, because people sail better when they know why. I crew on other boats whenever I can,
      mostly to steal ideas about sail trim.
    </p>
    <p>
      I’m on the management committee at <a href="https://dartmouthyachtclub.ca"
        >Dartmouth Yacht Club</a
      > for a little while longer, looking after web and communications. A Yachtmaster
      certification is on the list somewhere after the rigging and the engine.
    </p>
    <p>
      Otherwise: guitar, and amps that occasionally smoke. Cars, mostly Volkswagens. The current
      one is a 2024 Golf R after a long line of others, and I’ve learned German engineering means
      the check engine light comes on with great precision. Smart home projects that work
      fine until I improve them. And two cats: Ziggy, a calico with a talent for disapproval,
      and Ivee, an Abyssinian who treats the house as a test environment.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .path {
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .path ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .path li {
    padding: 0.85rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .path li.sub {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .path li.sub::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.35rem;
    top: 1.6rem;
    width: 0.6rem;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--faint);
  }
  .head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.25rem 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .role {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .role strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .sep {
    color: var(--faint);
  }
  .when {
    font-family: var(--meta-font);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--faint);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .note {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.925rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .kind {
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .quotes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }
  .more {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
